Logic :

Initialise left maxlen and c
iterate each number in for loop using right pointer
if the number (nums[right]) equal to 0
then increment c
if c greater than k 
move the left pointer until reduce c less than k , i.e., until you find another zero by the left pointer , because the condition states that the subarray contains at most k zeroes
calculate max length (right-left+1)

Code :


class Solution {
    public int longestOnes(int[] nums, int k) {
        int left=0;
        int maxlen=0;
        int c=0;
        for(int right=0;right<nums.length;right++){
            if(nums[right]==0){
                c++;
            }
            if(c>k){
                while(c>k){
                    if(nums[left++]==0){
                        c--;
                    }
                }
            }
            maxlen=Math.max(maxlen,right-left+1);
        }
        return maxlen;
    }
}
